      "raw_response": "ANSWER: SUPPORTED. The abstract suggests that SIV infection leads to a depletion of TH17 cells, which in turn results in impaired mucosal barrier function and increased dissemination of Salmonella Typhimurium from the gut. The depletion of TH17 cells and the subsequent weakened mucosal barrier is linked to increased dissemination of the bacteria, as shown by the increased systemic dissemination in IL-17 receptor\u2013deficient mice. This supports the claim that depletion of Th17 cells during SIV infection can lead to increased dissemination of Salmonella Typhimurium from the gut. The confidence level of this claim is high as it is based on experimental evidence involving gene expression profiles and the use of IL-17 receptor\u2013deficient mice.\n\nReferences:\n1. \"Mucosal interleukin-17 deficiency promotes Salmonella dissemination from the gut.\" Nature Communications, vol. 7, no. 10707, 2016. https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms10707",
